<title>USA: UK's Clarke rules out tax cuts unless justified.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke rules out tax cuts unless justified.</headline>
<text>
<p>WASHINGTON, Sept 29 (Reuter) UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kennth Clarke on Sunday said he had no intention of cutting taxes unless they were economically justified but would be prepared to tighten economic policy if there was inflationary pressure.</p>
<p>However, speaking to reporters during the annual IMF/World Bank meeting, Clarke reiterated that he was comfortable with his 2.5 percent growth target for this year.</p>
</text>
